        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(control-ui): improve session key display for direct chats with long identifiers",
        "body": "Related: #61213 (partial fix — issue stays open for full priority scheme)\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nLong direct-chat session identifiers (e.g. `ou_67075ec667cac0a7feae2c5094fd27b2`, 30 chars; `user_1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef`, 36 chars) overflow the Sessions table cells and details panel in Control UI, making sessions hard to identify at a glance. Users on feishu/telegram/dingtalk direct chats with long open_ids see a wall of opaque characters instead of a recognizable session label.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nScoped UI fix only — adds a dedicated `shortenSessionKeyForCell` helper in `ui/src/ui/session-display.ts`:\n\n- Truncates identifiers >20 chars to `first_6...last_4` format (e.g. `ou_670...27b2`)\n- Preserves full raw key in hover `title` attribute for debugging\n- Keeps canonical `parseSessionKey` **unchanged** — no API/contract changes\n- For non-direct keys (main/subagent/cron), defers to `parseSessionKey`'s fallback name directly (no prefix duplication)\n- Applies only to Sessions table cell + details panel title\n\n## Scope Clarification\n\nThis is a **partial fix for #61213**, addressing the immediate UI truncation need. The complete solution — full `binding.comment → agent.name → 技术标识符` priority scheme — is intentionally **out of scope** for this PR and should be tracked in a follow-up issue.\n\nIssue #61213 stays open to track the complete priority implementation. This PR lands the user-facing pain point fix first.\n\n## Data Model Compatibility\n\n**No persisted/serialized state changes.**\n\n- `shortenSessionKeyForCell` is a **pure display helper**, called only at render time in `renderRows()`\n- `parseSessionKey` (canonical parser) is **unchanged** — same input/output contract\n- No `JSON.stringify`, no `localStorage`, no config writes, no migration needed\n- No upgrade impact — existing sessions render identically except long direct-chat IDs are truncated in display\n\n## User Impact\n\n- Sessions table cells no longer overflow horizontally\n- Raw key still accessible via hover for debugging (no information loss)\n- Identity rows (with `friendlyKeyLabel`) keep existing behavior — only fallback rows get truncation\n- Short identifiers (≤20 chars) are unaffected\n- Non-direct sessions (main/subagent/cron) render cleanly without prefix duplication\n\n## Evidence\n\n### Unit tests\n- 21 new tests in `ui/src/ui/session-display.test.ts` (covers `parseSessionKey`, `shortenSessionKeyForCell`, `resolveSessionDisplayName`)\n- 26 existing tests in `ui/src/ui/views/sessions.test.ts` (all still passing)\n- **47 total passing** via `pnpm test -- ui/src/ui/session-display.test.ts ui/src/ui/views/sessions.test.ts`\n\n### Visual behavior proof\nThree screenshots in PR comments demonstrate the Sessions table cell, hover tooltip, and details panel paths after the fix. ClawSweeper assessed proof as 🐚 platinum hermit with media proof bonus.\n\n### Maintainer review\n@steipete reviewed and approved with explicit risk assessment:\n> \"Risk assessment: Low — Pure UI display change, no state/config/API modifications, comprehensive test coverage\"\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Related to #61213 (partial fix — issue stays open, NOT using \"Closes\" syntax)\n- [x] `pnpm build && pnpm check && pnpm test` passes locally\n- [x] 47 unit tests passing (21 new + 26 existing)\n- [x] No changes to `parseSessionKey` (canonical parser preserved)\n- [x] No persisted state changes (display-only)\n- [x] No unrelated Gateway protocol doc changes (reverted)\n- [x] No proof scripts committed (kept `scripts/` lint-clean)\n- [x] Fixed prefix-duplication bug for non-direct keys (Subagent/Cron)\n- [x] No `CHANGELOG.md` edit (per CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [x] Fork PR with \"Allow edits by maintainers\" enabled\n",
        "branch": "fix/issue-61213-session-display-id",
